// Title: Potential Persistence Via AppCompat RegisterAppRestart Layer
// Sigma ID: b86852fb-4c77-48f9-8519-eb1b2c308b59
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2024-01-01 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, persistence, T1546.011
// Description: Detects the setting of the REGISTERAPPRESTART compatibility layer on an application. This
//   compatibility layer allows an application to register for restart using the
//   "RegisterApplicationRestart" API. This can be potentially abused as a persistence mechanism.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate applications making use of this feature for compatibility reasons
// References:
//   - https://web.archive.org/web/20240115021338/https://github.com/nasbench/Misc-Research/blob/d114d6a5e0a437d3818e492ef9864367152543e7/Other/Persistence-Via-RegisterAppRestart-Shim.md
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/cb982537eb7397f93785ec066cce7b017050a43f/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_persistence_app_cpmpat_layer_registerapprestart.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.
// Note: 1 wildcard comparison(s) rewritten to 'matches regex' (KQL treats * in contains/endswith/== as a literal character)

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey matches regex @"(?i)\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\CurrentVersion\\AppCompatFlags\\Layers.*$" and RegistryValueData contains "REGISTERAPPRESTART"
